sections.body:
Two entry surfaces: the topo binary and the package-root index.ts barrel. The barrel re-exports server, bundle, pipeline, enrichment, and views.

Declared runtime module references:
@topo/diagram-core: workspace:*
@topo/enrichment: workspace:*
@topo/graph: workspace:*
@topo/languages: workspace:*
@topo/modules: workspace:*
@topo/reports: workspace:*
@topo/scanner: workspace:*
@topo/schema: workspace:*
@topo/site: workspace:*
@topo/story: workspace:*
@topo/views: workspace:*
@topo/workspace: workspace:*

The diagram singles out diagram-core so you can continue into its exposed rendering contract. Catalogue, snapshot, skills, and repository-generation helpers are not root exports and are not expanded here.

Root exports from views.ts:

buildCuratedViews; saveCuratedView; graphHash; parseSaveCuratedViewRequest;
serializeCuratedViewsSnapshot; serializeCuratedViewDeltas;
graphFromSiteBundle; augmentSiteBundle.

Contracts: CuratedViewsBuild, CuratedViewConflictError, CuratedViewMetadataError. Save requests and returned snapshots use @topo/views types; graph inputs use @topo/schema.

This is the exposed path-based curated-view surface, not arbitrary diagram authoring or a private implementation map.
